{:ts "2026-07-28T00:50:28Z", :kind :decision, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-opus-5", :dod "Make the reconstruction pipeline native to the event-sourcing process: event-ledger law in Malli, first Python tool ported to Clojure, and the bb/JVM runtime boundary settled by measurement.", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :host "local-shell", :manifest "src/fork_tales/law/reconstruction.cljc, docs/reconstruction/runtime-split.md, bb.edn, deps.edn", :refs "src/fork_tales/law/reconstruction.cljc, src/fork_tales/reconstruction/handoff.cljc, scripts/reconstruction/ledger.clj, scripts/reconstruction/validate.clj, test/fork_tales/reconstruction/handoff_test.clj", :tests "clojure -M:test green: 25 tests, 100 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (was 14/43 before this change). bb lane executed end-to-end against the real handoff-schemas.json: exit 1 on invalid packet, mu1 and mu6 both fired, 12 errors reported, :handoff/validated event appended and re-read through reconstruction.ledger with case id, uuid run id, and packet sha256. All relative links in docs/reconstruction verified to resolve (0 broken).", :decisions "libpython-clj cannot run under babashka — measured, not assumed: com.sun.jna.Native raises ClassNotFoundException in bb, and libpython-clj requires JNA plus dtype-next native interop. A babashka pod was rejected because a libpython-clj pod would itself be a JVM process, so it adds a bencode hop and a wrapper to maintain while buying nothing over a plain deps.edn alias. The DSP lane therefore lives behind clojure -M:metrics and the two runtimes communicate only by appending to ledgers/reconstruction.edn, which makes the ledger the IPC and keeps every lane independently replaceable. Handoff invariants mu1-mu6 were moved out of code into fork-tales.law.reconstruction/handoff-invariants as data, leaving the runtime a thin interpreter; validation logic was placed in a pure cljc namespace so it is testable on the JVM rather than only under bb.", :drift "audio_metrics.py is not portable to bb (librosa, matplotlib) and is additionally unrunnable as written: the referenced venv at references/mir-workbench/.venv does not exist, so a Python environment must be rebuilt before either route works. audio_grade.py and spectrogram_image_judge.py remain unported. The libpython-clj version pinned in the :metrics alias is unverified because Maven was unreachable from this sandbox and must be checked on first run. Three prior blockers stand unchanged: OpenUTAU patched exporter, demucs, gemma4:e4b-128k.", :note "Three real bugs were found and fixed by the new tests, not by inspection: error paths rendered a keyword's colon, absent keys threw NullPointerException via (name nil), and keyword-keyed EDN packets silently skipped every string-keyed schema check. Work performed in a throwaway clone; no writes to ~/spaces/fork_tales_v2 or to ~/Music."}
{:ts "2026-07-28T01:03:59Z", :kind :test-run, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-opus-5", :dod "Execute every reconstruction script against real committed evidence and repair what execution revealed.", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :host "local-shell", :manifest "docs/reconstruction/runtime-split.md, resources/reconstruction/contracts/fork_tales_audio_reconstruction.edn", :refs "scripts/reconstruction/validate.clj, scripts/reconstruction/audio_grade.py, scripts/reconstruction/spectrogram_image_judge.py, scripts/reconstruction/audio_metrics.py, scripts/reconstruction/audio_agent.cljs", :tests "validate.clj: exit 1 on invalid packet, 12 errors, mu1+mu6 fired, ledger event appended and re-read. audio_grade.py: reproduced committed grade.json exactly (all numbers identical after path normalisation). spectrogram_image_judge.py prompt and scores subcommands both ran; scores chained into the grader raised coverage 0.3104 -> 0.3560 and confidence 0.1406 -> 0.1610 while score moved only 0.2943 -> 0.3022, matching the operating model's claim that judges add coverage rather than score. audio_metrics.py compare reproduced committed metrics.json: 6 of 7 numeric metrics bit-identical, mel_db_correlation differing by 2e-9, both input sha256 matching. audio_agent.cljs ran under nbb: usage for 17 subcommands, and the metrics subcommand produced 8 artifacts plus :ok true end-to-end through the venv. clojure -M:test 25 tests / 100 assertions / 0 failures.", :decisions "Rebuilt the deleted metrics venv at ~/Music/fork-tales/references/mir-workbench/.venv with --system-site-packages rather than passing pip --break-system-packages, because PEP 668 blocks user installs on this host and breaking the OS python to run one grader is not an acceptable trade. Recovered the secret-scrub-corrupted literals from pre-purge git blob 2c85c7f39 rather than guessing them.", :drift "A historical secret purge had replaced the literals node and root with REDACTED_SECRET inside audio_agent.cljs, breaking the node:fs/node:path/node:child_process requires and the artifact-root and root-dir bindings, so the canonical runner could not start at all; handoff-schemas.json had publication_refs corrupted the same way. Both repaired from pre-purge blobs. The same corruption remains in docs/lyrics and ledgers/ingest.edn, which are corpus projection and append-only history and were left untouched. Correction to an earlier receipt: the metrics lane was reported unavailable on the basis of the missing venv; the real cause was that librosa 0.11 lazy-loads, so import succeeds while use fails on absent joblib. Demucs, the OpenUTAU patched exporter, and gemma4:e4b-128k remain unavailable.", :note "Evidence artifacts reference /home/err/devel/Music paths that no longer resolve, so re-running a grader on a committed evidence.json silently degrades coverage rather than erroring; verification used a path-translated scratch copy and left the committed artifacts unmodified."}
{:ts "2026-07-28T01:10:09Z", :kind :observation, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-opus-5", :dod "Close the loop: convert this session's friction into file-based spores and ledger entries so the lessons outlive the session.", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :host "local-shell", :manifest ".ημ/session-mycology/ledger.md, .ημ/session-mycology/spores/", :refs ".ημ/session-mycology/spores/20260727-200827-exercise-not-import-capability-probe.md, .ημ/session-mycology/spores/20260727-200827-recover-scrubbed-literals-from-pre-purge-blobs.md, .ημ/session-mycology/spores/20260727-200827-check-inputs-before-blaming-the-tool.md", :tests "sm-init.bb, sm-log.bb and sm-spore.bb executed; 4 ledger entries and 3 spores written and read back.", :decisions "Scored four phases separately rather than the session as a whole, because efficiency varied sharply across them: locating 0.8, consolidating 0.75, porting 0.7, verifying 0.4. Only phases scoring p-skill-candidate >= 0.7 produced spores, so the decoy-directory and provenance-versus-reproducibility observations were logged as ledger notes rather than promoted into spore files. Per protocol these spores are left :status incubating and were NOT self-promoted; promotion belongs to the spore-reviewer actor in a later session.", :drift "The sm-log.bb and sm-spore.bb scripts record the cwd as session identity, which was a throwaway clone path here and therefore useless to a future reader; the field was replaced with the repository identity before commit and the durable anchors are the commit refs in :receipt-refs. Worth fixing upstream in the session-mycology scripts.", :note "The verification phase scored worst on efficiency and highest on value: execution found a runner that could not start and a corrupted schema, both invisible to every prior read. The generalised lesson is recorded in the spores, and the assert-before-probing failure was folded into the existing verify-service