{:pi "eta-mu", :ts "2026-07-29T23:15:47.666Z", :host "local", :kind :fix, :origin "claude-code", :repo "/home/err/spaces/fork_tales_v2", :owner "pr-3-review-closeout", :note "PR #3: resolved the four remaining unresolved review threads. Includes a self-correction: the FSM change I made in e93a296 was a regression that froze the board's CLI write path, and the reply I posted claiming resolve-fsm supported it was wrong.", :tests "Empirical FSM probe on a throwaway board copy at scratchpad/fsmtest (single card, uuid 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111): (A) with {extends promethean, buildGateCommands [clojure -M:test]}, `eta-mu kanban frontmatter <uuid> status review` threw `transition rejected: No transition from 'in_progress' to 'review'`, and `status testing` failed identically -- every transition rejected, board frozen. (B) with \"promethean\", `status review` threw `transition rejected: Build gate failed: `pnpm build` exited with code 1` and `status testing` succeeded -- reproducing the original finding. (C) with a complete hand-authored FSM map in JSON gating both in_progress->review and testing->review on a build-gate check running clojure -M:test, the transition was silently ALLOWED (card reached status: \"review\", no gate output) because JSON string check ids never match the keyword lookup (get-in fsm [:checks :build-gate]) and evaluate-transition falls through to its :else allowed branch. After the fix: `eta-mu kanban count` returns 27 tasks (icebox 6, incoming 11, breakdown 4, ready 2, done 4); `clojure -M:test` ran 23 tests / 91 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors.", :refs "Installed engine: @eta-mu/rheos@0.1.0 bundled in volta eta-mu@1.1.1 at /home/err/.volta/tools/image/packages/eta-mu/lib/node_modules/eta-mu/node_modules/@eta-mu/rheos/dist/server.js, byte-identical (cmp) to the npx-cached copy. Its resolve_fsm is `fsm==null ? default_fsm : (\"promethean\"==fsm) ? promethean_fsm : map?(fsm) ? fsm : default_fsm` -- a map is returned VERBATIM as the FSM, with